On Saturday, November 2, 2013 1:50:50 PM UTC-4, pafcribe wrote: 
>
>  And in trying to get the flavor of the "even" part of the phrase, I 
> think it's a kind of mixture of "ca" and ".u".  But the form "ko'a broda 
> ko'e ca .u ko'i" is not valid.  It's possible to mix tags like "pu ca" or 
> "ca bai", but I guess logical connectives are different?
>
 
I don't know about tags, but you can do a tensed logical connection (CLL Ch 
14 <http://www.lojban.org/publications/reference_grammar/chapter14.html> - 
starting at about 18.4) to get the the "even" you want.  I think what 
you're looking for is:
 
"Justice be done" {.ijucabo} "Heaven falls."
 
ke'u, this does not put "Heaven falls" in a sumtcita tag off of the main 
bridi "Justice be done."  If you really want the "Heaven falls" to be an 
abstract sumti off of the main bridi, I would hazard a guess at saying 
"Justice be done" ?{gi'uca lo nu "Heaven falls" kei}  I'm supposing {gi'u} 
would "bridi-tail" it onto the main bridi, and {ca} would act as a 
sumtcita, expecting a single sumti, which would have to come in the form of 
an event (hence {lo nu...kei})
 
mi nintadni .iseni'ibo zoi gy. Take what I say with a grain of salt gy.
 
mi'e .neit. mu'o

